{"name":"Jacaranda","hex":"#f9d7ee","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Jacaranda","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Bignoniaceae – jacarandas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Jacaranda"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jacaranda","blocks":[{"text":"Jacaranda is a genus of 49 species of flowering plants in the family Bignoniaceae, native to tropical and subtropical regions of the Americas and cultivated around the world. The generic name is also used as the common name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Jacaranda_cuspidifolia_flower.jpg/330px-Jacaranda_cuspidifolia_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacaranda","wikidata":"Q311105"},{"title":"Jacaranda (Trevor Rabin album)","blocks":[{"text":"Jacaranda is the fifth studio album by South African musician, songwriter, and producer Trevor Rabin, released on 8 May 2012 on Varèse Sarabande. His first solo album of new material since Can't Look Away (1989), Rabin started work on the album in 2007 by writing music in various styles that was challenging for him to play, including jazz fusion, rock, blues, classical, and bluegrass. Most of the album's song titles refer to Rabin's experiences while growing up in South Africa. Recording took place over a six-year period at his studio in Los Angeles. Five guest musicians perform on the album, including drummers Lou Molino III, Vinnie Colaiuta, Rabin's son Ryan, bassist Tal Wilkenfeld, and singer Liz Constantine."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/98/TrevorRabinJacaranda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacaranda_(Trevor_Rabin_album)","wikidata":"Q11162496"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Jacaranda_leaves_Tel_Aviv.jpg/500px-Jacara